{
  "id": "proj-weight-plate-tree",
  "slug": "weight-plate-tree",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Weight Plate Tree",
  "summary": "A welded plate stand with six horns. Gets the plates off the floor and off your back.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 4,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Cut the 2x2 tube with the cutoff wheel: one 48 in upright, one 30 in base rail and two 14 in base stubs that will make a cross with the upright at its centre.",
    "Grind a bevel on every edge that will be welded and take the mill scale back to bright metal for 1 in around each joint. Never weld galvanized steel; the zinc fumes are toxic.",
    "Tack the cross base together flat on a level surface, square it with the magnetic squares, then stand the upright in the centre, check it plumb on two faces and tack it.",
    "Cut the threads off one end of each 1 1/2 in black pipe nipple. Its 1.9 in outside diameter fits the 2 in hole of Olympic plates.",
    "Mark three horns on each of two opposite faces at 10, 22 and 34 in, staggered side to side. Set each at 15 degrees upward with the angle finder so plates cannot slide off, tack it, re-check, then weld everything out in short runs, alternating sides to limit distortion.",
    "Grind sharp edges, wipe the steel clean, prime and paint it, push end caps into the open tube ends and stick rubber pads under the feet. Load the heaviest plates on the lowest horns."
  ],
